  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "Fixed `counter.mjs`.\n\n**What was wrong:** `current` was declared at module scope, so every counter shared the same state — creating a second counter overwrote the first, and increments leaked across instances.\n\n**The fix:**\n- Moved `current` inside `createCounter` as a closure variable, so each call gets its own independent state.\n- Kept the named export `createCounter` unchanged.\n- `initial` is validated as a finite number (throws `TypeError` before any state is created).\n- `increment`/`decrement` now validate `step` as a finite number and throw `TypeError` *before* mutating `current`, so a bad step leaves the counter unchanged.\n- Positive and negative finite steps work naturally via `+=`/`-=`.\n\nPublic tests were not modified.",
